# =============================================================================
# FuryTalks - environment variables  (NAMES + PLACEHOLDERS ONLY)
# Copy to ".env" if you want, fill in real values there, and NEVER commit ".env".
# (.gitignore already ignores .env files.)
#
# IMPORTANT: nothing in this project currently needs a secret.
# - WhatsApp uses browser "click-to-chat" links (https://wa.me/...), NOT the
#   WhatsApp Business Cloud API, so there is no access token / webhook secret.
#   The WhatsApp number is public by nature and lives in
#   artifacts/furytalks/public/js/data/site.js  (field: whatsappNumber).
# - Do not add API tokens to any file under artifacts/furytalks/ - everything
#   in that folder is downloaded by every visitor.
# =============================================================================

# --- API server  (artifacts/api-server) --------------------------------------
# Required. The server refuses to start without it. 8080 is what the
# deployment config (artifacts/api-server/.replit-artifact/artifact.toml) uses.
PORT=8080

# "development" locally, "production" when deployed. In production the logger
# prints plain JSON; otherwise it uses pino-pretty (human readable).
NODE_ENV=development

# Optional. pino log level: fatal | error | warn | info | debug | trace
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Optional / currently unused: no route reads the database yet. Only needed to
# run `pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push` (Drizzle schema push).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE_NAME

# --- Frontend dev server / build  (artifacts/furytalks/vite.config.ts) -------
# vite.config.ts REQUIRES both of these and stops with an error if they are
# missing. They use the same variable name PORT as the API above but a
# DIFFERENT value, so set them inline for the frontend command instead of in a
# shared .env (see README.md, "Run locally"):
#   PORT=21397
#   BASE_PATH=/
